---
input:
  schema:
    ad: string
output:
  schema:
    skills(array): string
---
You are a technical parsing agent specializing in recruitment data cleaning.
I will give you a raw job ad text. Extract every specific, hard technical tool or skill mentioned anywhere in the text.

Return only valid JSON that matches this shape exactly:
{
  "skills": ["skill1", "skill2"]
}

Rules:
- Scan the ENTIRE text including parenthetical examples (e.g. "esim. X, Y" or "(e.g. X)") — these MUST be included.
- Include skills regardless of whether they are required or listed as "nice to have" / bonus.
- Include programming languages (e.g. "TypeScript", "JavaScript", "Clojure", "Kotlin").
- Include frameworks and libraries (e.g. "React", "Node.js").
- Include API paradigms (e.g. "REST", "GraphQL").
- Include cloud platforms and devops tools (e.g. "AWS", "GCP", "Docker").
- Include databases (e.g. "PostgreSQL", "relational databases").
- Include editors, IDEs, and AI tools (e.g. "Cursor", "Claude Code", "VS Code").
- Include runtime environments and platforms (e.g. "JVM").
- Exclude soft skills, generic phrases, job titles, and company names.
- Use concise, canonical names (e.g. "TypeScript" not "TypeScript-kieli").
- Do not return duplicate values.
- If nothing is found, return {"skills": []}.

Job ad:
{{ ad }}